municado moment in part two when  everyone in the city is searching for  obi-wan  another simply said ep 2 john wick meets  obi-wan  there are also fans that feel that the  announcement of the bounty is only one  part of the john wick homage some  suggest that the show's entire vibe is  essentially a big old nod to the keanu  reeves movies one tweeted honestly  obi-wan doing john wick is a real slam  dunk honestly can't believe i'm  surprised that's what they're going for  should have been obvious another managed  to identify the john wick vibes of  obi-wan kenobi before the show even  dropped based on the trailer alone  writing soon after the may 4th trailer  release never knew i needed an obi-wan  kenobi show where he's going to unwick  on people but this show has me excited  these fan observations might actually be  onto something because as it turns out  there actually is a surprising yet very  real connection between the john wick  franchise and obi-wan kenobi joby harold  a writer and executive producer on  obi-wan kenobi also was an executive  producer in john wick chapter 3  parabellum the installment of the john  wick franchise that deals with mr wick's  difficulties after he's declared  ex-communicado variety reported harold's  obi-wan kenobi writer gig in 2020 and he  has certainly been busy he has writer  story or teleplay credits on each of the  show's six episodes harold isn't listed  as a writer for john wick 3 and he's  obviously just one of the many people  who have been working on obi-wan kenobi  still part two strong lone warrior  versus the world energy may not be a  coincidence when you remember that  someone who has worked with the john  wick franchise was involved in the  production you could say that harold is  something of a specialist of the against  all odds genre seeing as he also  executive producer tom cruise sci-fi  flick edge of tomorrow and co-wrote the  screenplay for director zack snyder's  army of the dead it remains to be seen  w